  "name": "chennai_urban_2015",
  "title": "Chennai urban flood (Nov-Dec 2015 pattern)",
  "description": "Extreme NE-monsoon rainfall over a city whose drainage is both undersized and partially clogged, compounded by tide lock: at high tide the storm drains cannot discharge to sea at all, so water ponds even as rainfall eases. Ponding rises with essentially no river signal, which is why a river-gauge-only flood model fails completely in urban settings.",
